1
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:13,940
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:19,920
Liu Sanhao!

3
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,360
I'll kill you!

4
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,240
Liu Sanhao!

5
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,680
I'll kill you!

6
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:27,440
I'll kill him!

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,760
Sorry, Officer!

8
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,520
Alright!

9
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:30,600
(Based on novel Doctor Qin: Executer)
I'll sit!

10
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,360
(Based on novel Doctor Qin: Executer)
Sorry!

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,560
Sorry!

12
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,800
Sorry. Sorry.

13
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,400
Can you behave yourself?

14
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,800
Yes, yes!

15
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:36,960
I can.

16
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:37,600
Yes.

17
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,000
I arranged

18
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,120
your mother's funeral for you.

19
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:53,000
With full honors.

20
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,600
Everything she deserved.

21
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,480
The cemetery is on the south slope.

22
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:58,920
Facing the sun.

23
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:02,400
Great view.

24
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,280
Mom.

25
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:05,720
Mom!

26
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:13,000
Thanks. Thank you.

27
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,080
Why... why is it you?

28
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:31,720
You recognized me?

29
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:32,640
Why?

30
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,760
I treated you so badly back then.

31
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,360
Because

32
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,800
we share a common enemy.

33
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:52,580
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 16=

34
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,720
Tests show

35
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,520
they came from the same printer.

36
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,400
(Personal Joint Liability Guarantee Contract)
After Jin Qingshan died,

37
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,360
(Debtor: Jin Qingshan, Guarantor: Jin Keke)
this guarantee became the trump card

38
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,800
the Liu Sanhao gang used
to hound Jin Keke.

39
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,480
(Serve the People with Dedication)
The loan kept compounding with interest.

40
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,880
By the time her father died,

41
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,200
it was already
an astronomical figure to them.

42
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:17,320
She was set up to be tied
to the debt for life.

43
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:18,880
After her father died,

44
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,160
all his debt fell on her.

45
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:23,520
So this was their excuse
to keep controlling,

46
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,560
threatening, and pressuring Jin Keke.

47
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,720
She had a motive

48
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:27,880
in this series of cases.

49
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,520
Yet every time a crime was committed,

50
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,320
she had an ironclad alibi.

51
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,600
We previously tried to prove

52
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,000
Jin Keke was at the crime scenes
when they happened.

53
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,960
So we were all trapped

54
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,120
in a dead end

55
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,480
by her airtight alibi.

56
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,960
But the appearance of the drone

57
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,120
shattered all her alibis.

58
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:44,960
All this only proves

59
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,560
she wasn't the executor
of those murders,

60
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:48,800
but it doesn't prove

61
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,920
she wasn't the mastermind behind them.

62
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:52,880
The start of all this

63
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,920
probably traces back

64
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,160
to that endless debt.

65
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:58,560
Jin Keke.

66
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,880
She must have been abused horribly

67
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,320
at Fengshan Villa,

68
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,680
just like those girls back then.

69
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,120
She had a blood feud

70
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:11,200
with every single victim.

71
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,040
So she could never

72
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,640
just be an accomplice in some case.

73
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,040
She's the mastermind

74
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:19,640
behind this whole revenge killing spree.

75
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,840
She wrote a murder script

76
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,840
for every person seeking revenge.

77
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,200
That's correct.

78
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,560
(Violence)

79
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:34,120
This was a trial filled
with a strong sense of ritual.

80
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,120
Each of them

81
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:38,480
died for their own crimes.

82
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,240
From a criminal psychology perspective,

83
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,240
these share the exact same mindset.

84
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,200
They could only come
from the same person.

85
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,040
She was the victim.

86
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:49,720
Qiao Shengchan

87
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:50,880
was the perpetrator.

88
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:52,520
How did they end up on the same side?

89
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:53,680
He was turned.

90
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,240
She used Qiao Shengchan's hatred
for Liu Sanhao

91
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,120
and handed him the ammunition
for his revenge.

92
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,720
She turned someone who once hurt her

93
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,360
into the most crucial and sharpest blade

94
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,920
in her revenge plan.

95
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:08,960
Alright.

96
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,560
(Serve the People with Dedication)
First, we need to

97
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,640
find evidence that she planned all this.

98
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:15,200
Second, we need to find her hiding spot.

99
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:15,960
Third,

100
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,960
we need to find her contact records
with these people.

101
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:18,920
There is a place...

102
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,720
you guys need to check out thoroughly.

103
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,200
What about you?

104
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,000
Mr. Dong, I'm requesting to be recused.

105
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,880
Because of your relationship
with Jin Keke?

106
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:39,920
Yes.

107
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,320
If it compromises fairness,

108
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:42,720
you should recuse yourself.

109
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:44,480
But your situation

110
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,600
isn't there yet.

111
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,120
Keep following up for now.

112
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,120
If anything new comes up later,

113
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,360
let me know anytime.

114
00:04:59,450 --> 00:05:00,720
Oh, my.

115
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,100
Well,

116
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,200
what's with all the officers?

117
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,720
Did something happen to Keke?

118
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,400
The convenience store owner reported

119
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,640
Jin Keke missing.

120
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,880
Do you know where she went?

121
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:13,040
She said

122
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,680
she's been feeling down lately

123
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:17,440
and went to stay with a friend
for a few days to clear her head.

124
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,640
I've called her and she won't answer.

125
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,720
I texted her and she hasn't replied.

126
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:24,480
She's... she just worries me so much.

127
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:28,920
This is a search warrant.

128
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,240
Mind if we look around inside?

129
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,000
Keke's a good girl.

130
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,000
You better hold on to her.

131
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,200
Did you do something

132
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,520
to upset her,

133
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,800
and now she's avoiding you?

134
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:55,640
Ms. Song,

135
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,200
do you really know nothing

136
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,040
about what's going on with Keke?

137
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,680
I know all about her stuff.

138
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:05,800
Back then,

139
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,240
after Wen's accident,

140
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,280
someone told me

141
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,080
Wen went out with Keke.

142
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,040
She must be hiding where Wen went.

143
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,080
I used to resent her.

144
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,000
I asked her

145
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,480
what happened that night.

146
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:35,920
Ms. Song, you wanted to see me?

147
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:41,040
Where were you the night

148
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,440
Wen had her accident?

149
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,680
I went to a friend's birthday party.

150
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,640
Weren't you with her?

151
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,720
No.

152
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,200
Someone saw you two

153
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,720
leave the school together.

154
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,440
We split up at the school gate.

155
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,240
Didn't she say where she was going?

156
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,360
No.

157
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,560
You're lying!

158
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,800
You're her best friend.

159
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:15,240
Being best friends

160
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:17,800
doesn't mean knowing everything
about each other.

161
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:19,800
Ms. Song,

162
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,280
I'm just as devastated
about Xia Wen as you are.

163
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,680
I can't sleep at night.

164
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,920
But I'm not a criminal.

165
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,240
Even if I were,

166
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,520
it's not your place to question me!

167
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:35,200
Later,

168
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:37,120
I ran into her at the hospital.

169
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,320
Honestly,
she was even worse off than I am.

170
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,640
I lost my daughter.

171
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:17,200
But her?

172
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:21,800
It was like her whole life
just ended right there.

173
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,680
She probably didn't do a thing.

174
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,280
A teenager

175
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:29,200
carrying a stigma like that

176
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:32,720
with everything falling apart at home,

177
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:34,720
how was she supposed to go on?

178
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:38,800
Later,

179
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,920
she kept coming to find me.

180
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,400
So I brought her home to live with me.

181
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,720
It's really not that complicated.

182
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:50,040
We just kept each other warm.

183
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,280
I treated her like Wen.

184
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,480
She treated me like a mom.

185
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,800
We just leaned on each other

186
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,200
and got through one day at a time.

187
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,240
Qin.

188
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,520
We've searched Jin Keke's room.

189
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:06,840
Want to take a look?

190
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:41,940
(Fundamentals of Accounting)

191
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:07,980
(Qin, Qin)

192
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,640
(Welcome to my world!)

193
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,200
(Let me show you around.)

194
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,800
(This is a picture you took of me.)

195
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
(I love it.)

196
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,840
(This is my stationery collection.)

197
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,520
(This is a gift you gave me)

198
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,800
(when I turned seventeen.)

199
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:02,040
(And the only time
you ever gave me a gift.)

200
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,320
(And right here.)

201
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:08,480
(I wrote all of these.)

202
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:10,200
(Most of them)

203
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,480
(are about you.)

204
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:15,840
(I was too shy to let you see.)

205
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,440
(So every time I finished writing,)

206
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,640
(I tore them up.)

207
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:24,960
(Qin Ming.)

208
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:31,200
(I love talking with you
on the rooftop.)

209
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:37,440
(I love how you always competed
with me on exam scores.)

210
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:41,440
(I love the books you like to read.)

211
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,280
(I love it
when you write letters to me.)

212
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,520
(I...)

213
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,280
(I like you.)

214
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,640
What are you guys doing?

215
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,440
What are you doing
in my daughter's room?

216
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,840
Why are you in my daughter's room

217
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,440
instead of out chasing bad guys?

218
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,480
Ms. Song. Ms. Song.

219
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,520
Ms. Song, calm down.

220
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:21,640
Did something happen to Wen?

221
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,640
Please calm down.

222
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,640
Are you a police officer?

223
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:24,840
I am.

224
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:26,600
Then why are you in Wen's room

225
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,520
instead of out chasing bad guys?

226
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,280
Get out!

227
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:30,000
Ms. Song!

228
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,960
Sorry to bother you!

229
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,120
Let's go!

230
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:32,400
Go!

231
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:32,720
Sorry!

232
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,320
Go catch the bad guys!

233
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:34,880
Sorry to disturb you.

234
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,840
Bring Wen back to me!

235
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:41,040
Go catch the bad guys!

236
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,440
Bring Wen back!

237
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:49,280
Wen!

238
00:13:03,530 --> 00:13:04,280
Hey.

239
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,080
Detective Ming,

240
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:06,680
let me ask you about a case.

241
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:08,840
Qin Ming.

242
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,320
What is it?

243
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:11,640
Tell me,

244
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:15,400
if a girl is really nice,

245
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:17,920
pure as a blank sheet of paper,

246
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,720
but

247
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,640
she's forced

248
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:23,400
to do

249
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,200
bad things

250
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:27,280
because of things

251
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,880
she can't control,

252
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:34,120
like protecting her family

253
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,080
or just trying to survive,

254
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:39,640
does that mean

255
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,800
she's no longer worthy of being loved,

256
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,840
even if she had no choice?

257
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,920
Does that mean
she can never wash herself clean?

258
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:57,120
Even if she does
a ton of good things after that,

259
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,640
people will still

260
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,200
think of her

261
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:06,000
as a bad girl.

262
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:07,640
Right?

263
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:10,720
If

264
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:14,640
that blank sheet

265
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,320
got stained because it got caught

266
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,680
in a mudslide,

267
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,800
then it's not the paper that's dirty.

268
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,680
It's the mudslide.

269
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:26,280
Besides, that girl used to be so good.

270
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:27,880
She's the one

271
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:30,240
who got hurt the most by all of this.

272
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,480
What she needs right now

273
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,640
isn't someone to judge her.

274
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,920
She needs someone to reach out,

275
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,440
take her hand,

276
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:39,800
and tell her

277
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,640
it's not her fault.

278
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,000
Got it!

279
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,240
I'll remember what you said,

280
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,280
Detective Ming.

281
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:07,520
Hey,

282
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:09,120
you haven't answered me yet.

283
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,840
Who's the last person we're going after?

284
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:14,240
Is it Chen Xiaolong, the guy

285
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,200
who beat up Su Qingchen
with Liu Sanhao back then?

286
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,720
Or is it Li Mazi, the loan shark?

287
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,280
Neither.

288
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,640
At least tell me.

289
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:28,680
Do you need money?

290
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:29,680
Money?

291
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:31,720
Who doesn't need money?

292
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:37,640
You mean...

293
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:40,040
You mean we can get our hands
on a lot of money?

294
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:57,880
Jin Qingshan!

295
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:00,640
Yo.

296
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:01,480
Feeding her medicine, huh?

297
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,440
The hell with the medicine!

298
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,520
You gonna pay up or not?

299
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,880
You old fossil, why aren't you dead yet?

300
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,000
I'll pay. I swear I'll pay.

301
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:08,760
I'll pay.

302
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:09,640
Jin Qingshan.

303
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:11,840
You've got five days!

304
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:12,480
Yeah, yeah.

305
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,160
Okay. Got it.

306
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,400
That's just a warning.

307
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,680
If you don't pay up,

308
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:17,800
just you wait.

309
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:19,040
Let's go!

310
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:22,680
Mom. Mom.

311
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:23,960
It's okay.

312
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,720
It's okay. It's alright.

313
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:25,520
It's fine.

314
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,160
Mom.

315
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:27,000
It's alright.

316
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:39,620
(Mourning)

317
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,600
It doesn't matter who's next.

318
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:56,600
My life is yours.

319
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,720
Just say the word,

320
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:59,600
and I'll send him down
to join Liu Sanhao.

321
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:03,260
(4; 7)

322
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:04,660
(21)

323
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:06,740
(Do Not Cross; Police)

324
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:10,680
(Do Not Cross; Police)
The body's burned to a crisp.

325
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:11,600
The face is charred.

326
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,160
No way to confirm the identity.

327
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,480
Male or female?

328
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:15,680
Not Jin Keke.

329
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:17,520
Male.

330
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,320
Burn injuries on the body
are unevenly distributed.

331
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:31,760
Head, chest, and upper limbs
are severely charred.

332
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,360
Lower limbs, back, and buttocks

333
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:36,000
are relatively intact.

334
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,000
It's blast trauma.

335
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:50,300
(Do Not Cross; Police)

336
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:54,360
There are third to fourth degree burns
on the trunk and limbs.

337
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:57,200
The skin is completely charred
and leathery.

338
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,720
Some muscles are exposed and contracted.

339
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,080
The burn areas
have relatively clear boundaries.

340
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:04,080
The dorsal side is relatively preserved.

341
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:06,320
That's typical of burning on the ground.

342
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,520
Qin, is this...?

343
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,480
Are you gonna ask me

344
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,360
if this is Qiao Shengchan?

345
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:19,740
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

346
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:24,380
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

347
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:28,620
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

348
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:32,940
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

349
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:45,860
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

350
00:18:45,860 --> 00:18:48,660
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

351
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:52,980
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

352
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:57,180
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

353
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:01,940
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

354
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:06,380
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

355
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:10,740
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

356
00:19:10,740 --> 00:19:14,820
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

357
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:27,980
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

358
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:32,300
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

359
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:36,100
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

360
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,020
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

361
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:43,780
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

362
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:48,460
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

363
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,740
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

364
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:52,820
♪We stop here in this night♪

365
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:57,260
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

366
00:19:57,260 --> 00:20:03,500
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

367
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:11,860
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

368
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:30,180
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

369
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:38,540
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪
